a company out of nowhere and

00:22:38.008 --> 00:22:41.250
that had no reference outside of Brazil.

00:22:41.250 --> 00:22:47.696
So I think the cool part was to go and
come back and be an actor of change and

00:22:47.696 --> 00:22:52.217
try to change somethings
that really annoyed me.

00:22:52.217 --> 00:22:56.649
The experience that we had in Brazil and
the opportunity to fix a problem here.

00:22:56.649 --> 00:22:59.806
And that it was opportunity for
me and also a responsibility.

00:22:59.806 --> 00:23:05.415
Because I felt empowered to take
everything that I had learned there,

00:23:05.415 --> 00:23:07.323
the network that I had.

00:23:07.323 --> 00:23:11.107
Then come back and
kind of bring to Brazil and to Latin,

00:23:11.107 --> 00:23:14.317
something that could
impact many lives here,

00:23:14.317 --> 00:23:19.683
most probably much more different than I
would have done if I stayed in the US.

00:23:19.683 --> 00:23:23.285
The hard part was that everything
is harder in Latin, and

00:23:23.285 --> 00:23:25.246
everything is lower in Latin.

00:23:25.246 --> 00:23:29.904
So there, you talk to a bunch of
people and they want to invest.

00:23:29.904 --> 00:23:34.259
Here, nobody wanted to invest in us and we
spent many, many years just bootstrapping

00:23:34.259 --> 00:23:38.081
with, by the way, a few friends from
Stanford that were the first angels.

00:23:38.081 --> 00:23:42.965
But it took a while for us to really have
a series a shitload of money coming in,

00:23:42.965 --> 00:23:45.610
which is a very different reality today.

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:49.965
And also hard to find talent that just
as I talked to, we were doing that for

00:23:49.965 --> 00:23:53.354
the first time,
we had no real idea of what we were doing.

00:23:53.354 --> 00:23:58.951
And I would have paid
a lot more if I could find

00:23:58.951 --> 00:24:04.330
talent that That would show me
a little bit of the way and

00:24:04.330 --> 00:24:08.026
we had to learn almost
everything from scratch.

00:24:08.026 --> 00:24:12.977
I think this is also changing but
it still is a big difference

00:24:12.977 --> 00:24:18.136
from doing business in Brazil,
or lot on comparing to the US.

00:24:22.456 --> 00:24:25.580
&gt;&gt; Anybody has a different, I want to
ask that question to each one of you.

00:24:25.580 --> 00:24:27.460
It's an important one.

00:24:27.460 --> 00:24:31.926
What's the hardest part of going
back to that diamond working versus

00:24:31.926 --> 00:24:33.620
staying in the US for you?

00:24:33.620 --> 00:24:34.934
&gt;&gt; I was going to say like,

00:24:34.934 --> 00:24:38.670
I think that the personality
of Latin Americans is amazing.

00:24:38.670 --> 00:24:40.729
It's warm, it's foreign.

00:24:40.729 --> 00:24:45.299
It's outgoing, so building personal
relationships in Latin America is great.

00:24:45.299 --> 00:24:49.486
But the way we organize ourselves
as societies is still far from

00:24:49.486 --> 00:24:52.251
being perfect and that's a challenge for

00:24:52.251 --> 00:24:57.639
everybody's daily life when you compare
it to the US or you compare it to Europe.

00:24:57.639 --> 00:25:02.646
And that imposes challenges on
on how you raise your family

00:25:02.646 --> 00:25:08.279
differently on how you live daily
security issues in the region.

00:25:08.279 --> 00:25:13.489
Or social issues in the region so
in to some extent it's

00:25:13.489 --> 00:25:20.075
a trade off on the quality of life and
the quality of life you can lead.

00:25:20.075 --> 00:25:26.009
That's also very challenging that's
also what makes doing something for

00:25:26.009 --> 00:25:31.753
the region like inspiring and want to
make once makes you want to do more but

00:25:31.753 --> 00:25:36.475
it's but it's a challenge,
it's a personal challenge.

00:25:36.475 --> 00:25:40.070
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I would add, for
me there is no playbook,

00:25:40.070 --> 00:25:46.064
when you look at the US what was going on
in Silicon valley for entrepreneurship.

00:25:46.064 --> 00:25:51.004
There was some guidelines that
would tell you want to raise money.

00:25:51.004 --> 00:25:53.661
It's going to hear you want to
include talent in your team,

00:25:53.661 --> 00:25:55.024
you kind of do these things.

00:25:55.024 --> 00:25:58.802
Here at least five years ago there was
nothing you had to kind of make up

00:25:58.802 --> 00:26:00.310
everything along the way.

00:26:00.310 --> 00:26:05.200
And I would also add that when you want to
solve one problem in Latin America and

00:26:05.200 --> 00:26:09.799
you start solving it, you need to
solve like a hundred surrounding it.

00:26:09.799 --> 00:26:12.619
Like if you want to say I want to
start a company to sell phones and

00:26:12.619 --> 00:26:15.603
then you realize okay, but
there's no connection to the wire and

00:26:15.603 --> 00:26:17.678
then I need to add
the connection to the wire.

00:26:17.678 --> 00:26:20.137
Okay, but now there's no this, no post and

00:26:20.137 --> 00:26:23.670
you have to have everything around
to make your business work.

00:26:23.670 --> 00:26:26.838
That if you probably would have, if I
would have seen that USA would have said,

00:26:26.838 --> 00:26:30.020
okay, I'm only going to focus on this and
then everything around kind of works.

00:26:30.020 --> 00:26:32.130
And it's going to kind of
help me to the environment.

00:26:32.130 --> 00:26:34.234
Here you have to assume
nothing around works and

00:26:34.234 --> 00:26:35.764
you're going to have to solve it to.

00:26:35.764 --> 00:26:39.200
So you're going to have to build a lot
of expertise around your main core

00:26:39.200 --> 00:26:44.308
business,
&gt;&gt; I would say,

00:26:44.308 --> 00:26:47.690
sorry, we're saying something Mickey.

00:26:47.690 --> 00:26:49.556
&gt;&gt; Go ahead, Marcos.

00:26:49.556 --> 00:26:50.973
&gt;&gt; Sorry
&gt;&gt; So,

00:26:50.973 --> 00:26:55.967
I will say what first of all I think
Latin America is changing a lot.

00:26:55.967 --> 00:26:57.752
And very fast I think it's important for

00:26:57.752 --> 00:27:01.127
everyone to have that in mind because
many of the things that were very hard.

00:27:01.127 --> 00:27:06.116
For example like getting funding or
finding good technical talent,

00:27:06.116 --> 00:27:10.504
although things have improved a lot,
and very, very fast,

00:27:10.504 --> 00:27:14.740
obviously, they're still a war on talent,
etc.

00:27:14.740 --> 00:27:19.410
But the same thing happens,
everywhere in the world today.

00:27:19.410 --> 00:27:22.240
So many things have changed for
the better.

00:27:22.240 --> 00:27:24.932
Having said that, I would say,

00:27:24.932 --> 00:27:30.280
the unpredictability of
Latin America is just incredible.

00:27:30.280 --> 00:27:35.225
It's incredible and the longer you operate
in the region and in the more countries

00:27:35.225 --> 00:27:40.250
that you operate, the more impressed you
are by how unpredictable things are.

00:27:40.250 --> 00:27:45.560
And that obviously is fun, that is very
fun on the one hand but it's very hard.

00:27:45.560 --> 00:27:52.780
It makes it very hard because,
it's unpredictable in many different ways.

00:27:52.780 --> 00:27:58.820
And, it can be very hard to build
businesses for the long term.

00:27:58.820 --> 00:28:05.866
It's sometimes it's politics, sometimes
it's unions, sometimes its judges.

00:28:05.866 --> 00:28:10.608
Regulatory frameworks you end
up encountering things that you

00:28:10.608 --> 00:28:14.011
would never dream of
encountering in the US.

00:28:14.011 --> 00:28:15.936
Maybe once every 20 years,

00:28:15.936 --> 00:28:19.489
in Latin America you encounter
five of those per year.

00:28:19.489 --> 00:28:25.145
So that in my opinion Is probably one
of the hardest things to build and

00:28:25.145 --> 00:28:29.060
grow a business for
the long term in the region.

00:28:29.060 --> 00:28:32.241
And I don't see unfortunately,
I don't see that changing for

00:28:32.241 --> 00:28:34.650
the better I see changing for the worse.

00:28:34.650 --> 00:28:35.642
For example,

00:28:35.642 --> 00:28:41.480
one of our most predictable perhaps
our only predictable market was Chile.

00:28:41.480 --> 00:28:44.302
And all of a sudden Chile now has become,

00:28:44.302 --> 00:28:47.378
nobody knows where Chile
is going not know.

00:28:47.378 --> 00:28:53.858
So it's a it's interesting that's
something that you will not

00:28:53.858 --> 00:28:58.818
definitely not find in the US or in Europe
&gt;&gt; I'm going to I like

