does anybody remember the score?

00:29:24.509 --> 00:29:26.610
&gt;&gt; What's the GMAT?

00:29:26.610 --> 00:29:30.630
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:29:30.630 --> 00:29:34.650
But-

00:29:34.650 --> 00:29:36.997
&gt;&gt; As expected it was hard It was really

00:29:36.997 --> 00:29:41.693
hard but I hit harder than the GMAT
was the first three months at school,

00:29:41.693 --> 00:29:46.719
trying to really be able to talk and
understand that you read half the speed.

00:29:46.719 --> 00:29:49.319
And when you write your write
like a quarter of the speed.

00:29:49.319 --> 00:29:53.669
It takes a lot of pushing and willpower
and headaches to be able to try to stay

00:29:53.669 --> 00:29:57.340
at the level in which you can
actually contribute to the class.

00:29:57.340 --> 00:30:03.010
I don't know, the rest of you agree
&gt;&gt; And it's not only the classes,

00:30:03.010 --> 00:30:08.009
because the classes are more formal,
more organized, so, if you're used to

00:30:08.009 --> 00:30:13.030
reading and writing, and maybe not so
used to talking, but you can get going.

00:30:13.030 --> 00:30:17.015
The social life is also very draining,
you go to a bar in It's loud and

00:30:17.015 --> 00:30:21.790
everybody's talking over each other and
make jokes that you don't understand.

00:30:21.790 --> 00:30:25.741
So it's kind of you think that
you go out and you relax but

00:30:25.741 --> 00:30:30.718
you come back like exhausted nd then
you have to keep talking about it.

00:30:30.718 --> 00:30:35.420
But get used to it so it's part of
life and after the pains one of

00:30:35.420 --> 00:30:40.404
the benefits as well
&gt;&gt; There's a lot

00:30:40.404 --> 00:30:44.741
of questions going back to
